    {
      "key": "methodology",
      "title": "Algorithm and methodology",
      "status": "available",
      "source": "llm_draft",
      "text": "The model is a logistic regression fitted in R as a GLM with binomial family and logit link, using 21 predictors (LIMIT_BAL, EDUCATION, MARRIAGE, PAY_0 and PAY_2 to PAY_6, BILL_AMT1 to BILL_AMT6, PAY_AMT1 to PAY_AMT6), with SEX and AGE excluded from the predictors and reserved for fairness analysis, and no scaling or encoding applied. Data is validated (30,000 rows, 25 columns, no missing values, default rate between 0.20 and 0.24) and split into stratified 80% train and 20% test sets with random_state 42, although these are stated as defaults and the orchestration code confirming the actual split, seed and data source is not documented. Predictions are classified at a fixed 0.5 threshold, and the reported results show ROC AUC of about 0.707, accuracy of 0.809, precision of about 0.694, recall of about 0.244 and a Brier score of about 0.147. A parity check against a statsmodels implementation is reported as an overall pass, with a maximum probability difference of about 3.6e-07 against a tolerance of 1e-05.",
      "rows": []
    },
