      "key": "limitations",
      "title": "Limitations and assumptions",
      "status": "available",
      "source": "llm_draft",
      "text": "Categorical codes such as EDUCATION, MARRIAGE and the PAY_* status variables enter the GLM as numeric values, imposing linear effects, and the justification for this treatment and for the variable choices is not documented. The 0.5 threshold is not calibrated to the roughly 22% base rate or to business costs, and its rationale is not documented; the reported recall of about 0.244 indicates most defaulters are not flagged at this threshold. Excluding SEX and AGE does not prevent proxy discrimination, and the reported age-group disparate impact is about 0.767 (about 0.907 for sex). A synthetic demo dataset can be substituted when the UCI data is unavailable and would produce a materially different model, and no monitoring plan, retraining frequency or performance triggers are documented.",
      "rows": []
    },
